# Generated skill mirrors. The single human-authored source is
# skills/<name>/SKILL.md; these two trees are byte-identical copies produced by
# `make skills` (tools/skills_sync.py) and pinned by tests/arch/test_skill_drift.py.
# Do not hand-edit — edit the source and regenerate. `linguist-generated`
# collapses them in GitHub diffs and keeps them out of language stats.
#
# `eol=lf` pins these to LF in the working tree on every platform. The CLI
# `go:embed`s cli/internal/skillgen/content/*.md into the binary, so a Windows
# checkout converting them to CRLF (core.autocrlf) would embed CRLF bytes and
# break the frontmatter parser (splitFrontmatter also normalizes defensively).
# The source SKILL.md files are pinned too so the mirrors stay byte-identical.
cli/internal/skillgen/content/*.md linguist-generated=true eol=lf
src/jentic_one/shared/web/content/*.md linguist-generated=true eol=lf
skills/**/SKILL.md eol=lf

